@@ -90,0 +91,20 @@ Most command line options have corresponding X resource, see doc/alttab.ad for e
+  * `-g` <NUMBER>:
+    resource: alttab.group
+    default: <0>
+
+    Group windows by their case-insensitive `WM_CLASS` application class. <NUMBER> must be between 0 and 2:
+
+      <0>: Show every window.
+
+      <1>: Show the most recently used window from each application.
+
+      <2>: Show only windows from the application active when the switcher opens.
+
+    Windows without `WM_CLASS` remain separate.
+
+  * `-f`:
+    resource: alttab.focus
+    default: no
+
+    Focus and raise each selected window while the switcher remains open. Escape restores the original selection.
+
